.TH MU2E-NODE-INVENTORY 1 "2026-09-29" "mu2edaq-power-recovery 0.2.0" "Mu2e DAQ Operations"
.SH NAME
mu2e-node-inventory \- print the Mu2e DAQ node inventory used by the recovery tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2e-node-inventory
.RB [ \-l
.IR LOCATION ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR CLASS ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR NETWORK ]
.RB [ \-\-hostnames ]
.RB [ \-\-protected ]
.RB [ \-\-validate ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the node inventory that
.BR mu2e-power-recovery (1)
will use, read from
.BR mu2edaq-topology.yaml (5).
It contacts nothing.
.PP
When a run reports something unexpected about a machine, the first question is
whether it knew about that machine at all, and with which interfaces. This
answers that, from the same file the phases read, so its answer is the phases'
answer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-l " LOCATION" "\fR, \fP" \-\-location " LOCATION"
Limit to a location:
.BR mc2 ", " mc1 " or " teststand .
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-c " CLASS" "\fR, \fP" \-\-class " CLASS"
Limit to a host class:
.BR gateway ", " manager ", " datalogger ", " dcs ", " cfo ", " tracker ,
.BR calorimeter ", " crv ", " stm ", " extmon ", " worker ", " teststand .
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-n " NETWORK" "\fR, \fP" \-\-network " NETWORK"
Limit to nodes present on this network, and with
.B \-\-hostnames
print that network's interface names rather than the lab names.
.TP
.B \-\-hostnames
Print bare hostnames, one per line, for piping into
.BR pssh (1)
or a shell loop.
.TP
.B \-\-protected
List only the hosts protected from destructive IPMI commands.
.TP
.B \-\-validate
Check the inventory and the power sequence instead of listing nodes, across
every location (not only
.IR topology.locations ).
Each finding is an
.BR error ,
a
.B warning
or an
.BR info .
Errors: the topology does not load, an invalid hostname (the same rule the
loader applies), a subnet that is not a network, a power-sequence stage in an
unknown location. Warnings: a location with no nodes (with its
.IR status ", " owner " and " inventory_source
metadata), a BMC with no lab host, a subnet shared or overlapping between
locations, a gateway or protected host that is not in the inventory, a stage
naming a node not in its location's inventory, inventory nodes that no stage
covers. Info: a populated location with no stage at all. With
.B \-\-json
the result is one object
.RI { topology ", " findings ", " counts ", " ok }.
Validation is never run when the topology is loaded, so an incomplete
inventory (MC-1) does not stop a run.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the full inventory as JSON, including each node's class, location,
per-network interface names and subnets.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Main configuration file. Default:
.IR config/power-recovery.yaml .
It is read for
.IR topology.file " and " topology.locations ,
so pointing this at the configuration a run used shows that run's inventory.
.TP
.BI \-\-env\-file " FILE"
Dotenv file. Default:
.IR config/.env .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Warnings and errors only.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the option summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Everything the tools know about:
.RS
.EX
mu2e-node-inventory
.EE
.RE
.PP
The MC-2 tracker nodes:
.RS
.EX
mu2e-node-inventory \-l mc2 \-c tracker
.EE
.RE
.PP
BMC names for a sweep, piped into the C++ prober:
.RS
.EX
mu2e-node-inventory \-n ipmi \-\-hostnames | mu2e-probe \-\-port 623
.EE
.RE
.PP
Which hosts may never be powered off:
.RS
.EX
mu2e-node-inventory \-\-protected
.EE
.RE
.PP
Gaps and inconsistencies, before and after editing the topology:
.RS
.EX
mu2e-node-inventory \-\-validate
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The inventory was printed; with
.BR \-\-validate ,
there was no error finding (warnings allowed).
.TP
.B 1
With
.BR \-\-validate :
at least one error finding.
.TP
.B 2
The topology file is missing, malformed, or the location is unknown.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2e-power-recovery (1),
.BR mu2edaq-topology.yaml (5),
.BR mu2e-probe (1)
.SH AUTHOR
A. Norman <anorman@fnal.gov>, Mu2e DAQ Operations.
